-- "inter-classes" -- a genuine inter-level class, System, declared
-- directly in the multi-model, owned by no single constituent model.
-- That's exactly the one case where a BARE class name (simpleType) is
-- correct inside inter-constraints/inter-associations, contrasted right
-- here with Graph@Node, which -- because it DOES belong to one specific
-- model -- still needs the usual Model@Class (multiType) qualification.
-- See the reverted-fix note in project memory for why the bare-name
-- rejection on Graph@Node's kind of reference is deliberate, not a bug.

MLM InterClassHub

model Graph

class Node
end


inter-classes
class System
attributes
  name: String
end


inter-associations
association Contains between
  System[1] role owner
  Graph@Node[*] role elements
end


inter-constraints
context System inv SystemHasAName:
  self.name <> ''


mediator Graph < NONE
end
